  "id": "Compound::DB01595 - Gene::2557",
  "verbalization": "Nitrazepam is likely to interact with Gabra4 through a mechanism involving the Gaba receptor system. The evidence suggests that Nitrazepam binds to Gabrd, a subunit of the Gaba receptor, which in turn participates in Gaba receptor activity. This activity is then participated by Gabra4, indicating a potential functional link between Nitrazepam and Gabra4. The varying scores across the paths reflect the strength of the interactions, with Nitrazepam binding to Gabrd in all cases, suggesting a consistent interaction site. The presence of multiple paths pointing to Gabra4 as a participant in Gaba receptor activity supports the hypothesis that Nitrazepam modulates Gaba receptor function, potentially through Gabrd. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Nitrazepam in influencing Gaba receptor activity, which may underlie its pharmacological effects.",
